{"name":"Crimson Strawberry","hex":"#9f2d47","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crimson","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep, slightly bluish red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a deep red colour.","Immodest. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crimson"},{"term":"strawberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sweet, usually red, edible accessory fruit of certain plants of the genus Fragaria.","Any plant of the genus Fragaria (that bears such fruit)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the flavor of strawberries.","Flavored with ethyl methylphenylglycidate, an artificial compound which is said to resemble the taste of strawberries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strawberry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crimson","blocks":[{"text":"Crimson is a rich, deep red color, inclining to purple. It originally meant the color of the kermes dye produced from a scale insect, Kermes vermilio, but the name is now sometimes also used as a generic term for slightly bluish-red colors that are between red and rose. It is the national color of Nepal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Maple_Leaf_Red_Ground_2000px.jpg/330px-Maple_Leaf_Red_Ground_2000px.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crimson"},{"title":"Strawberry","blocks":[{"text":"The garden strawberry is a widely grown hybrid plant cultivated worldwide for its fruit. The genus Fragaria, the strawberries, is in the rose family, Rosaceae. The fruit is appreciated for its aroma, bright red colour, juicy texture, and sweetness. It is eaten either fresh or in prepared foods such as jam, ice cream, and chocolates. Artificial strawberry flavourings and aromas are widely used in commercial products. Botanically, the strawberry is not a berry, but an aggregate accessory fruit. Each apparent 'seed' on the outside of the strawberry is actually an achene, a botanical fruit with a seed inside it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Garden_strawberry_%28Fragaria_%C3%97_ananassa%29_single2.jpg/330px-Garden_strawberry_%28Fragaria_%C3%97_ananassa%29_single2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strawberry"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Oaxaca_de_Ju%C3%A1rez%2C_detalles_07.jpg/500px-Oaxaca_de_Ju%C3%A1rez%2C_detalles_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Oaxaca_de_Ju%C3%A1rez%2C_detalles_07.jpg/500px-Oaxaca_de_Ju%C3%A1rez%2C_detalles_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOaxaca_de_Ju%C3%A1rez%2C_detalles_07.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/California_Palace_of_the_Legion_of_Honor_120_2015-01-03.JPG/500px-California_Palace_of_the_Legion_of_Honor_120_2015-01-03.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/California_Palace_of_the_Legion_of_Honor_120_2015-01-03.JPG/1280px-California_Palace_of_the_Legion_of_Honor_120_2015-01-03.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/California_Palace_of_the_Legion_of_Honor_120_2015-01-03.JPG/500px-California_Palace_of_the_Legion_of_Honor_120_2015-01-03.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACalifornia_Palace_of_the_Legion_of_Honor_120_2015-01-03.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Crimson_sunset_in_Wuhan_%282025